**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests`
- `kit-acceptance`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`

**How to implement.** The buttons for step 425's messages, in the study view's own files (001 §O 'Study view'; .spec-md §4 'New surfaces live in their own files'; AGENTS.md 'The button and the test send the same message'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S12.1. (1) Ids: `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, beside the study view's fixed ids (step 414): `static member studySessionGrid : ConstructorUiId = ConstructorUiId "StudySessionGrid"`; `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, beside `studyParameterRow` (step 414): `studySessionGainChoice (session : SessionName)`, `StudySessionGain_<FileStem.ofText of the session's text>` (step 24's file-stem rule, as the other derived ids), and `studyFitModeChoice (mode : FitMode)`, `StudyFitMode_<mode.value>`, each documented in one line; and `type SessionGainModel with member this.caption : ControlCaption`: `Free`, `Anchored to <the anchors' names, comma-separated>` and `Interpolated from <opening> to <closing>`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyUnknownsView.fs`, `studyUnknownsView` (step 414): after the unknowns grid, for the chosen study, the semi-bold `Sessions and gains:` and a `Grid` carrying `studySessionGrid`, three `Auto` columns `Session`, `Experiments` and `Gain`, a semi-bold header row and one row per `study.sessionsIn model.kitExperiments` (step 358): its name, its experiments' names comma-separated, and a `ComboBox` carrying `studySessionGainChoice session.name` over `session.gainModelOffers model.kitExperiments` (step 425) by `caption`, `study.gainModelOf session.name` selected, enabled while `model.kitWrites` offers writes (step 185), whose choice sends `StudyCommand (SetSessionGainModel (study.name, { session = session.name; model = <the chosen> }))`. A study of no session shows `This study's experiments form no session.`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyFitView.fs`, `studyFitView` (step 415): directly before the Run row, `Fit mode:` and one box per `FitMode.all` carrying `studyFitModeChoice mode` with `mode.text`, the study's `settings.mode` an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground` and the other a `MaterialsWindowView.verbButton` (step 241's chosen-option look), each sending `StudyCommand (SetFitMode (study.name, mode))`, shown only while writes are offered; under a read-only kit the line `Fit mode: <its text>`. The Run buttons are unchanged: the stage they send decides what a run fits, and the mode is what the study and its fit runs record (step 391). No other control changes. (4) Tests, mounted as `StudyViewTests` mounts its screens (step 414) over `TestAppScope.studyKitIn` with E1 and E3 set to `CalibrationRun` by `SetExperimentRole`: `each session of the study offers its gain models, and choosing one sends SetSessionGainModel`: the Unknowns step's `StudySessionGrid` holds `Session 1` with `E1, E2, E3` and a `StudySessionGain_Session 1` box offering `Free`, `Anchored to E1, E3` and `Interpolated from E1 to E3`, `Free` selected; choosing the anchored one dispatches `StudyCommand (SetSessionGainModel (QZ-LR, { session = SessionName "Session 1"; model = AnchoredSessionGain [ E1; E3 ] }))`; `the Fit step's mode choice sends SetFitMode`: the Fit step shows `StudyFitMode_1` chosen and pressing `StudyFitMode_2` dispatches `StudyCommand (SetFitMode (QZ-LR, StagedFit))`; `the study view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also checks `studySessionGrid`, `studySessionGainChoice (SessionName "Session 1")` and `studyFitModeChoice StagedFit`; `ScrollExtentTests`' `the kit window's Unknowns step leaves everything reachable` also reaches the sessions grid; and `KitWindowTests`' `a read-only window withholds every write control` also finds the gain box disabled and no `StudyFitMode_<n>` box.

**Acceptance.** After the view lands, the Unknowns step MUST list the study's sessions with a gain choice sending `SetSessionGainModel`, and the Fit step MUST offer the fit mode sending `SetFitMode`, both withheld from a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `each session of the study offers its gain models, and choosing one sends SetSessionGainModel`, `the Fit step's mode choice sends SetFitMode` and the widened `the study view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the kit window's Unknowns step leaves everything reachable` and `a read-only window withholds every write control`, the count rising by 2; kit-acceptance MUST pass over `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s41 invariants MUST pass.
